      "id": 1,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in 1879 spurred settlement and led to Leland being platted on July 15, 1887.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/leland_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Leland was named for founder John D. Thompson, who moved the post office from Benson's Grove and shortened the original name Lelandsburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leland%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first general store in Leland opened in 1880 when Pat Mahar relocated a store building to the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
